  <data name="Tour1_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Welcome to Orkeon Studio</value></data>
  <data name="Tour1_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Studio is the desktop companion of the orkeon CLI: edit appsettings.json through validated forms, then launch crews and watch the streamed log. This short tour walks through each part.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour2_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Two workspaces</value></data>
  <data name="Tour2_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Configuration covers the settings file — presets, typed sections, mounts, the raw JSON and a doctor diagnostic. Launch is where you run crews and browse the launch history.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour3_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>The settings file, always in sight</value></data>
  <data name="Tour3_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>This card shows which appsettings.json you are editing and whether it validates. It stays visible on every screen, so you always know what a save will touch.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour4_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>File actions</value></data>
  <data name="Tour4_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>New, open, reload, validate, save — the file-level actions live here on every configuration screen. Validation runs the same checks the runtime applies at load.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour5_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Start from a preset</value></data>
  <data name="Tour5_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>The same catalogue as orkeon init: Ollama, Docker Model Runner, OpenAI, any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, or none. Applying only pre-fills the Llm form — you review, then save.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour6_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Know which file wins</value></data>
  <data name="Tour6_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>The runtime walks four steps to find its settings. This card shows the whole chain and marks where your save target sits — no more silent surprises from a file next to the crew.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour7_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Sandboxed file access</value></data>
  <data name="Tour7_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Mounts are the only folders agents can see. Pick the physical folder, the virtual path agents get, and the rights — read-only by default, with per-sub-path overrides.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour8_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Launch and watch</value></data>
  <data name="Tour8_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>The exact command line is built live from your options. Dry-run validates without side effects; Run streams the log here, line by line, and ends with the exit code.</value></data>
  <data name="Tour9_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>When something is off</value></data>
  <data name="Tour9_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>The diagnostic runs orkeon doctor: binary, settings file, LLM reachability, mounts. Green means go; warnings tell you what to fix before a run fails.</value></data>

